{"availability":"available","full":"magicleap/SuperGluePretrainedNetwork","name":"SuperGluePretrainedNetwork","description":"SuperGlue: Learning Feature Matching with Graph Neural Networks (CVPR 2020, Oral)","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":4093,"forks":759,"created":"2020-03-17T19:32:12Z","updated":"2024-08-30T23:50:47Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["deep-learning","feature-matching","graph-neural-networks","pose-estimation"],"demo":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.07629","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.784Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.784Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.784Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.784Z","stars":4093,"forks":759}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SuperGlue is a CVPR 2020 research project done at Magic Leap. The SuperGlue network is a Graph Neural Network combined with an Optimal Matching layer that is trained to perform matching on two sets of sparse image features. This repo includes PyTorch code and pretrained weights for running the SuperGlue matching network on top of SuperPoint keypoints and descriptors. Given a pair of images, you can use this repo to extract matching features across the image pair.","SuperGlue operates as a \"middle-end,\" performing context aggregation, matching, and filtering in a single end-to-end architecture. For more details, please see:","We provide two pre-trained weights files: an indoor model trained on ScanNet data, and an outdoor model trained on MegaDepth data. Both models are inside the weights directory. By default, the demo will run the indoor model."],"features":["Full paper PDF: SuperGlue: Learning Feature Matching with Graph Neural Networks.","Authors: Paul-Edouard Sarlin, Daniel DeTone, Tomasz Malisiewicz, Andrew Rabinovich","Website: psarlin.com/superglue for videos, slides, recent updates, and more visualizations.","hloc: a new toolbox for visual localization and SfM with SuperGlue, available at cvg/Hierarchical-Localization. Winner of 3 CVPR 2020 competitions on localization and image matching!"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/magicleap/SuperGluePretrainedNetwork/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"b592252d2e603879fe6b6403170659743621c6248047a1cf943e68629d30feec","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.852Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.852Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"SuperGlue is a CVPR 2020 research project done at Magic Leap. The SuperGlue network is a Graph Neural Network combined with an Optimal Matching layer that is trained to perform matching on two sets of sparse image features. This repo includes PyTorch code and pretrained weights for running the SuperGlue matching network on top of SuperPoint keypoints and descriptors. Given a pair of images, you can use this repo to extract matching features across the image pair.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/magicleap/SuperGluePretrainedNetwork/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"b592252d2e603879fe6b6403170659743621c6248047a1cf943e68629d30feec","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/magicleap/SuperGluePretrainedNetwork/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.852Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-08-30T23:50:47Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/magicleap/SuperGluePretrainedNetwork/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.853Z","hash":"b592252d2e603879fe6b6403170659743621c6248047a1cf943e68629d30feec","originalBytes":19116,"storedBytes":19116,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["pairs","image","match","images","test","resize","demo","evaluation","superglue","run","assets","data","matching","scannet","pairs.py","dump","outdoor","input","provide","viz","see","matches","results","yfcc","following","keypoints","phototourism","click","default","exif","expand","ground","npz","repo","set","truth","auc","note","path","should","